WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.982 --> 00:00:14.021
Marcus Bell: Morning, both. Kyle, uh, I see you're on the road, so we'll keep this moving. So, Ashley, how's fall treating you?

2
00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:19.507
Ashley Moore: Busy. Aeration season plus termites, which is a fun combo. How about you?

3
00:00:20.423 --> 00:00:27.122
Marcus Bell: Good, good. Last QBR of the month for me, so so you're getting the tired version.

4
00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:38.535
Kyle Brennan: You're on speaker, by the way. I'm between the Cary shop and the Apex one, so if it cuts out, it's a dead zone on 64.

5
00:00:39.052 --> 00:00:45.199
Marcus Bell: No problem. I pulled the numbers for the quarter, want me to walk through the top level first?

6
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:46.644
Ashley Moore: Yeah, please.

7
00:00:47.944 --> 00:01:01.596
Marcus Bell: So total tracked calls across the six locations were up about 14% versus the same quarter last year. Google Ads is still your biggest source by volume, and the aeration landing page is, let me see, second.

8
00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:08.277
Kyle Brennan: That tracks. We pushed more budget into the fall campaign, so I'd hope it's up.

9
00:01:09.203 --> 00:01:19.705
Ashley Moore: The thing I actually look at is the signal breakdown. Appointment booked is up, quote given is up, so the leads look real, not just more calls.

10
00:01:20.336 --> 00:01:26.513
Marcus Bell: Right, and that's what I wanted to show you. Signal volume on booked appointments was up 19%.

11
00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:31.820
Kyle Brennan: Okay, that's good. Hold on, sorry, someone's honking at me. Go um, ahead.

12
00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:35.604
Marcus Bell: You're fine. Ashley, anything stand out on your side?

13
00:01:36.258 --> 00:01:47.373
Ashley Moore: One thing, and it's small but it's been bugging me. Saturday mornings, when people call about termites, a bunch of those get marked as spam and they're real.

14
00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:52.640
Marcus Bell: Okay. Is it the swarm calls specifically, or any Saturday call?

15
00:01:53.359 --> 00:02:05.170
Ashley Moore: Mostly the ones where the caller is kind of frantic, short call, they don't give a lot of info. I think the signal just doesn't have enough to go on.

16
00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:08.043
Marcus Bell: Got it. How many are we talking, roughly?

17
00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:20.499
Ashley Moore: I'd say eight or ten a Saturday over the last month. Not huge, but those are people with an active swarm in their wall, so they're not nothing.

18
00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:33.941
Marcus Bell: Yeah, that's real money walking away. Can you send me two or three call IDs from last Saturday? I want to look at what the transcript looks like on those.

19
00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.704
Ashley Moore: Yeah, I can pull those this afternoon.

20
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:47.641
Marcus Bell: Perfect. I'll take it to the team and see what we're working with. I don't want to guess at it from here.

21
00:02:48.653 --> 00:02:59.609
Kyle Brennan: Appreciate that that. And listen, while we're on it, CallRail called me again. They say their Google Ads sync is same-day, and I'll be honest, that got my attention.

22
00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:05.905
Marcus Bell: Fair. What's driving it, the timing of the conversions landing in Google Ads?

23
00:03:07.036 --> 00:03:15.976
Kyle Brennan: Part of it. I just don't like feeling like I'm behind on the bidding side when a competitor's telling me they're a day ahead.

24
00:03:17.398 --> 00:03:22.103
Ashley Moore: He gets a call from somebody every couple months. I mostly ignore them.

25
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.289
Kyle Brennan: I mostly ignore them too. This one just landed different.

26
00:03:27.908 --> 00:03:45.950
Marcus Bell: Understood. I'm not going to argue with you on it. What I can do is get you the actual picture on how your conversions are flowing into Google Ads right now, and then you can decide if the timing matters for your campaigns.

27
00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:53.270
Kyle Brennan: That's all I'm asking. I don't want a sales pitch, I want to know what's actually happening.

28
00:03:53.878 --> 00:03:57.776
Marcus Bell: Right. I'll pull that and follow up with you directly.

29
00:03:58.318 --> 00:04:05.700
Kyle Brennan: Okay. Sorry, I gotta take this other call, it's the Apex manager. Ashley, you got the rest?

30
00:04:06.815 --> 00:04:08.052
Ashley Moore: I got it.

31
00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:10.709
Kyle Brennan: Marcus, talk soon.

32
00:04:11.226 --> 00:04:12.550
Marcus Bell: Yep, take care.

33
00:04:13.475 --> 00:04:16.169
Ashley Moore: He does that. Okay, where were we.

34
00:04:17.181 --> 00:04:25.004
Marcus Bell: We were on signals, and we can stay there or move to whatever you want. How's the day to day with the platform?

35
00:04:26.459 --> 00:04:33.688
Ashley Moore: Honestly, the call summaries are the first thing I read every morning, they save me so much time.

36
00:04:35.183 --> 00:04:40.874
Marcus Bell: Good to you know, hear. Do you read them per location or all together?

37
00:04:41.862 --> 00:04:51.544
Ashley Moore: All together first, you know, then I drill into Raleigh and Cary if something looks off. It's like a ten minute scan instead of listening to twenty calls.

38
00:04:52.383 --> 00:04:56.794
Marcus Bell: And the rest of it, tracking numbers, routing, all behaving?

39
00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.598
Ashley Moore: Yeah, it's fine. No complaints there.

40
00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:08.159
Marcus Bell: Good. Anything on the the Google Ads side from your end, besides the timing thing Kyle raised?

41
00:05:08.482 --> 00:05:17.093
Ashley Moore: No, that's the one. I mean, I'd love for him to stop taking those calls, but that's not a product thing.

42
00:05:17.722 --> 00:05:26.735
Marcus Bell: Ha, yeah, that one's on you. So on the spam mislabels, walk me through what you do now when you catch one.

43
00:05:27.553 --> 00:05:35.927
Ashley Moore: I just flag it in my own spreadsheet and move on. I didn't know if there was anything to actually do about it.

44
00:05:36.719 --> 00:05:45.421
Marcus Bell: Okay. So send me the call IDs and I'll dig in. If it's a pattern on Saturday mornings specifically, that's useful for us to know.

45
00:05:46.896 --> 00:05:51.033
Ashley Moore: Will do. I'll put them in an email so you have them.

46
00:05:51.457 --> 00:05:55.406
Marcus Bell: Perfect. Anything else on your list before we wrap?

47
00:05:55.744 --> 00:06:00.846
Ashley Moore: That's it, really. The season's going well, we're just trying to keep up.

48
00:06:01.161 --> 00:06:09.189
Marcus Bell: That's a good problem. I'll send the recap today with the numbers and the two follow-ups, the call IDs and the Google Ads timing.

49
00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:13.599
Ashley Moore: Great. And I'll get you those calls by end of day.

50
00:06:14.216 --> 00:06:18.145
Marcus Bell: Sounds good. Tell Kyle I said good luck with the drive.

51
00:06:19.459 --> 00:06:20.801
Ashley Moore: I will. Thanks, Marcus.

52
00:06:21.921 --> 00:06:23.612
Marcus Bell: Thanks, Ashley. Talk soon.
